# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# Without this, `docker build` uploads target/ -- hundreds of megabytes of
# compiled classes and a fat jar -- into the daemon on every build, and the
# COPY of src/ risks picking up host-built artefacts that were compiled by a
# different JDK than the one in the build stage. The image must be built from
# source inside the container, not from whatever happens to be on the machine.
target/
!target/*.jar.original

# Local tooling and editor state
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Anything carrying secrets must never enter the build context
*.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test and coverage output
**/surefire-reports/
**/failsafe-reports/
**/jacoco*.exec

# The ground-truth corpus is a build artefact of the seed profile, not an
# input to the image.
ground_truth_labels.csv
